+/// How many clean workspace qubits one uncontrolled 54-AND product needs at this width.
+///
+/// One sub-product window at a time: at each level the low, high and middle sub-products are
+/// computed one after another into a window of 2*ceil(n/2)-1 qubits, reduced straight into the
+/// target and measured back to zero before the next is allocated, so the peak is that window
+/// plus the peak of the level below it -- 19 qubits at GF(2^12) rather than the 42 a whole
+/// 2n-1-bit product window needed.
+size_t gf_mul54_workspace_size(size_t degree);
+
+/// Adds the product of two GF(2^m) registers into a third one, with 54 ANDs at m=12.
+///
+/// As pseudocode:
+///     Q_target ^= Q_lhs * Q_rhs  (mod the field polynomial)
+///
+/// This is the same operation as gen_gf_mul, using the bilinear algorithms the exact
+/// search in `scripts/study_circuit_designer_directions.py` established as minimal at
+/// two and three bits (mu(2) = 3, mu(3) = 6, both by exhaustion) instead of the
+/// Karatsuba recursion's base case. Composed by Karatsuba, `12 = 3 * 3 * 6` gives 54
+/// ANDs against the built-in 63.
+///
+/// Every AND's target is cleared with `del_and` (a measurement plus a classically
+/// conditioned phase fixup, no Toffoli), and the product window with `mr`, so the
+/// AND count is also the Toffoli count of the product: 54 against 63.
+///
+/// The structure follows gen_gf_mul: an uncontrolled product accumulates directly into
+/// Q_target through a clean window, while a controlled one computes the product into a
+/// clean temporary, adds it in under the control, and clears the temporary for free with
+/// gen_gf_unmul (which measures the temporary and fixes up the phase, and is independent
+/// of how the product was computed).
+///
+/// Requires:
+///     Q_target, Q_lhs, and Q_rhs all have size field.degree(), and are pairwise disjoint.
+///     ctx.clean_workspace has at least gf_mul54_workspace_size(degree) qubits,
+///     plus field.degree() more when the operation is controlled.
+///
+/// Not upstream: this routine depends on the `MR` instruction added by
+/// `scripts/kickmix_mr_opcode.patch`, because it measures its windows back to zero
+/// rather than uncomputing them.
+void gen_gf54_mul(
+    CircuitBuilder &builder,
+    const CircuitGenCtx &ctx,
+    const GF2Field &field,
+    stride_span<const QubitId> Q_target,
+    stride_span<const QubitId> Q_lhs,
+    stride_span<const QubitId> Q_rhs,
+    QubitOrTrue control = true);
+
+}  // namespace kickmix
+
+#endif
